    v=d['arcs'][1]['vessel'];oldhazard=v['highAtmosphere']
    v['highAtmosphere']='NEW local encounter hazard above10000ft: nonmagical upper-atmosphere inhalation exposure, with a cold-inhalation damage component and a thin-air environmental-fatigue component. The errant equation causes melody loss, not this air hazard. These classifications and the following source-interface completions are proposed authorship requiring GPT review; they are not recovered climate rules or real atmospheric simulation. An unprotected breathing creature tracks actual cumulative exposure. At each completed60unprotected seconds, make one CONsaveDC15 for the event: failure3d6cold and oneExhaustion from the thin-air component; successhalfcold and noExhaustion. Roll cold damage once for this recipient/event and apply its actual save result, defenses and life rules. Partial exposure carries across short protected intervals; one uninterrupted protected minute clears only its incomplete remainder, not prior damage or Exhaustion. Actual no-breath permission, working cabin/airlock protection or an active compatible hood prevents this complete local inhalation event while effective. It grants no immunity to independent external cold, pressure, falling or other hazards. Partial defenses do not stop the exposure clock or cancel an already resolved event. No second unnamed suffocation track or arbitrary breath-holding timer is imported; the source corpus does not supply that missing full procedure in this review.'
